lication; not a novelty claim</data></edge><edge id="e462" source="deim-2009" target="area:sparse"><data key="relation">bridges_field</data><data key="epistemic_status">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence">Uses a reduced basis and selected entries to cheaply approximate nonlinear terms.</data><data key="evidence_url">https://laertes.caam.rice.edu/tech_reports/2009/TR09-05.pdf</data><data key="evidence_locator">Broad field classification based on stated method/application; not a novelty claim</data></edge><edge id="e463" source="stable-cs-2005" target="area:sparse"><data key="relation">bridges_field</data><data key="epistemic_status">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence">Establishes stable sparse-signal recovery from incomplete noisy linear measurements under conditions on the measurement matrix.</data><data key="evidence_url">https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0503066</data><data key="evidence_locator">Broad field classification based on stated method/application; not a novelty claim</data></edge><edge id="e464" source="sparse-operators-2012" target="area:sparse"><data key="relation">bridges_field</data><data key="epistemic_status">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence">Identifies structured linear operators from probing signals under conditions on their spreading-function support.</data><data key="evidence_url">https://arxiv.org/abs/1209.5187</data><data key="evidence_locator">Broad field classification based on stated method/application; not a novelty claim</data></edge><edge id="e465" source="sindy-2015" target="area:sparse"><data key="relation">bridges_field</data><data key="epistemic_status">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence">Fits sparse combinations of candidate nonlinear functions to discover dynamical equations from data.</data><data key="evidence_url">https://arxiv.org/abs/1509.03580</data><data key="evidence_locator">Broad field classification based on stated method/application; not a novelty claim</data></edge><e